CC The glasses the bundled optical elements are made of, in the Zemax AGF catalog format (docs/plans/physoptics-optical-materials.md)
CC Read by src/optic_glass.cpp. Lines: NM name formula MIL nd vd exclude status melt; CD the formula's coefficients (lambda in um);
CC LD the valid range in um; IT lambda (um), internal transmittance, thickness (mm); TD the thermal data, kept but not used.
CC
CC Sources. Schott glasses (N-BK7, N-SF11, N-SF10, N-F2, F2, N-SF6, N-SF1): the Schott optical glass data sheets, Sellmeier 1
CC (formula 2), as collected by refractiveindex.info (CC0). N-BK7's internal transmittance is the data sheet's 10 mm column,
CC rounded. UV fused silica (Corning 7980): Malitson 1965. CaF2: Malitson 1963. MgF2 (ordinary ray): Dodge 1984. Sapphire
CC (ordinary ray): Malitson and Dodge 1972. nd and vd are the formula's own values at the helium d line and the F and C lines.
CC
CC The coating oxides (SIO2, TA2O5, TIO2, HFO2, AL2O3) are thin films, whose index depends on how they were deposited: these
CC are Cauchy fits n = A + B / lambda^2 to typical evaporated films (n at 550 nm: Ta2O5 2.12, TiO2 2.31, HfO2 1.99, Al2O3 1.65),
CC written as Schott formulas (a0 = A^2, a2 = 2 A B, a3 = B^2). They are what the coating presets are designed with, not data
CC for any one vendor's process. SIO2 is the fused silica formula.
CC
CC ND-OD1 is a synthetic neutral density glass for tests: N-BK7's index with an internal transmittance of 0.1 through 2 mm at
CC every wavelength, an optical density of 1.
